      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it\u0027s fine to fix this. The costructor doesn\u0027t have any annotations for this field so this field may be null or non-null. I think that\u0027s why we left a TODO in the constructor.\n```\n   // TODO: Check whether mMatchSubscriberIds \u003d null or mMatchSubscriberIds \u003d {null} when\n   // mSubscriberId is null`\n```\nIf the mSubscriberIdMatchRule is SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_ALL then it won\u0027t care about the subscriberIds.\nIf the mSubscriberIdMatchRule is SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_EXACT then the subscriberId still need to match even it\u0027s null.\nThus I think whether a template should match null subscriberId depends on the subscriberIdMatchRule.\n\nDoes this answer your question?",
